    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10">The Atlantic Devil Ray occurs in coastal waters, reef areas, and also breakwaters. </font></color>
    </cell>
	<cell width="32" pady="10">
		<img src="ui/zoopedia/fact-bullet.tga" sx="0" sy="0" sw="32" sh="32" />
	</cell>    
    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10">The Devil Ray generally stays in waters with temperatures of 75-77 degrees </font></color>
    </cell>
	<cell width="32" pady="10">
		<img src="ui/zoopedia/fact-bullet.tga" sx="0" sy="0" sw="32" sh="32" />
	</cell>            
    <cell width="202" pady="10">
     <color r="255" g="255" b="255"><font name="Malgun Gothic" size="10">The Atlantic Devil Ray occurs almost exclusively on the American coast, however, there are a couple of groups that have been recorded in Africa</font></color>     
    </cell>
  </cell>
